  "notes": "USAGE:\nAt Japanese clinics and hospitals, patients typically fill out a {問診票|もんしんひょう} (medical questionnaire) before seeing the doctor. This form asks about symptoms, allergies, current medications, and medical history. The doctor then follows up with verbal questions during the {問診|もんしん}.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {問診票|もんしんひょう}: medical questionnaire\n- {問診|もんしん}を{受|う}ける: to undergo a medical interview\n- {問診|もんしん}する: to conduct a medical interview\n- {予診|よしん}: preliminary examination (similar but broader)",
